#
# description : This .audit is designed against the CIS VMware vSphere 8.0 ESXi STIG Benchmark v1.0.0
#
#<ui_metadata>
#<display_name>CIS VMware vSphere 8.0 ESXi STIG v1.0.0 CAT III Unix</display_name>
#<spec>
#  <type>CIS</type>
#  <name>VMware vSphere 8.0 ESXi STIG</name>
#  <profile>CAT III</profile>
#  <version>1.0.0</version>
#  <link>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23619</link>
#</spec>
#<labels>agent,cis,vmware_esxi_8.0_bare_metal</labels>
#<benchmark_refs>800-53,800-53r5,CAT,CCI,LEVEL,Rule-ID,STIG-ID,Vuln-ID</benchmark_refs>
#</ui_metadata>

<check_type:"Unix">

<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "VMkernel found"
      cmd         : "uname -a"
      expect      : "VMkernel"
    </custom_item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "CIS_VMware_vSphere_8.0_ESXi_STIG_v1.0.0_CAT_III_Unix.audit from CIS VMware vSphere 8.0 ESXi STIG v1.0.0"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23619"
      show_output : YES
    </report>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.35 ESXI-80-000207"
      info        : "The ESXi host Secure Shell (SSH) daemon must be configured to not allow gateway ports.

GROUP ID: V-258763
RULE ID: SV-258763r959010

SSH Transmission Control Protocol (TCP) connection forwarding provides a mechanism to establish TCP connections proxied by the SSH server. This function can provide convenience similar to a virtual private network (VPN) with the similar risk of providing a path to circumvent firewalls and network Access Control Lists (ACLs). Gateway ports allow remote forwarded ports to bind to nonloopback addresses on the server."
      solution    : "From an ESXi shell, run the following command:

esxcli system ssh server config set -k gatewayports -v no

or

From a PowerCLI command prompt while connected to the ESXi host, run the following commands:

$esxcli = Get-EsxCli -v2
$arguments = $esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.CreateArgs()
$arguments.keyword = 'gatewayports'
$arguments.value = 'no'
$esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.Invoke($arguments)"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-258763r959010_rule,STIG-ID|ESXI-80-000207,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-258763"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23619"
      file        : "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*(?i)GatewayPorts(?-i)[\\s]"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*(?i)GatewayPorts(?-i)[\\s]+no[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.37 ESXI-80-000210"
      info        : "The ESXi host Secure Shell (SSH) daemon must set a timeout count on idle sessions.

GROUP ID: V-258765
RULE ID: SV-258765r959010

Setting a timeout ensures that a user login will be terminated as soon as the \"ClientAliveCountMax\" is reached."
      solution    : "From an ESXi shell, run the following command:

esxcli system ssh server config set -k clientalivecountmax -v 3

or

From a PowerCLI command prompt while connected to the ESXi host, run the following commands:

$esxcli = Get-EsxCli -v2
$arguments = $esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.CreateArgs()
$arguments.keyword = 'clientalivecountmax'
$arguments.value = '3'
$esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.Invoke($arguments)"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-258765r959010_rule,STIG-ID|ESXI-80-000210,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-258765"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23619"
      file        : "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*(?i)ClientAliveCountMax(?-i)[\\s]"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*(?i)ClientAliveCountMax(?-i)[\\s]+3[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.38 ESXI-80-000211"
      info        : "The ESXi host Secure Shell (SSH) daemon must set a timeout interval on idle sessions.

GROUP ID: V-258766
RULE ID: SV-258766r959010

Automatically logging out idle users guards against compromises via hijacked administrative sessions."
      solution    : "From an ESXi shell, run the following command:

esxcli system ssh server config set -k clientaliveinterval -v 200

or

From a PowerCLI command prompt while connected to the ESXi host, run the following commands:

$esxcli = Get-EsxCli -v2
$arguments = $esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.CreateArgs()
$arguments.keyword = 'clientaliveinterval'
$arguments.value = '200'
$esxcli.system.ssh.server.config.set.Invoke($arguments)"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|3M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-258766r959010_rule,STIG-ID|ESXI-80-000211,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-258766"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23619"
      file        : "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*(?i)ClientAliveInterval(?-i)[\\s]"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*(?i)ClientAliveInterval(?-i)[\\s]+200[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>
  </then>

  <else>
    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "CIS_VMware_vSphere_8.0_ESXi_STIG_v1.0.0_CAT_III_Unix.audit from CIS VMware vSphere 8.0 ESXi STIG v1.0.0"
      info        : "NOTE: Nessus has not identified that the chosen audit applies to the target device."
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23619"
      show_output : YES
    </report>
  </else>
</if>

</check_type>
